The '''Relic Doge Base''' is an animated [[Enemy Bases|Enemy Base]] that only appears in [[Uncanny Legends]] and [[Zero Legends]]. It first appears in [[Cats in the Stars]], the final stage of [[Morningstar Isle]]. It was added in [[Version 9.7 Update|Version 9.7]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Relic Doge Base
|image = E 522.png
|first appearance = '''UL''': [[Cats in the Stars|Sub-chapter 26 - Cats in the Stars]]
|latest appearance = '''ZL''': [[Putrid Prison|Sub-chapter 13 - Putrid Prison]]
|money drop = N/A
}}

==Enemy==
This base can do a very weak attack from 2000 range that will [[Curse|curse]] all cats in its range. Like other animated bases, it is immune to all effects besides [[Surge Attack|Surges]] and [[Explosion]]s, and is a [[:Category:Typeless Enemies|Typeless]] enemy, not a [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]].

==Strategy==
[[:Category:Cats with Curse Immunity|Curse-immune cats]] are helpful along with any [[:Category:Resist Curse Cats|Resist Curse Cats]] if you have spare NP lying around. These aside, the Relic Doge Base has two other weaknesses. Its curse lacks 100% uptime, and so leaves your units with a window of opportunity, more so if you time them well. In all its appearances one can simply choose to fight outside of its range, preventing it from spoiling an attack. Units that can fire [[:Category:Surge Attack Cats|Surges]] and/or [[:Category:Explosion Cats|Explosions]] can deal some extra damage to it, due to the aforementioned lack of Immunity to those abilites.

